what threat does Russia pose to the UK  it's a question the cross-party  Intelligence and Security Committee of  MPs has been looking at examining topics  including espionage subversion and  possible attempts by Russia to interfere  in votes like the brexit referendum with  the face of the leave campaign now in  Downing Street Boris Johnson is the man  who will give final sign-off to the  report the committee says that should  have happened on Thursday number-10 says  it usually takes six weeks this is  completely untrue they're talking about  the six week process by which you clear  it through the agencies and the Cabinet  Office we're not talking about this  we're talking about the final clearance  by the Prime Minister and I really get  worried when an authoritative voice like  number 10 starts putting out these  completely bogus arguments with MPs due  to leave this place next week to start  campaigning Tuesday is the final chance  for the report to be published before  the election it should be released and I  suspect that the reason it hasn't been  published is they're going to try and  delay it past the dissolution of  Parliament on Tuesday in there they can  hide it away until some point in the  future if a report has been called for  and written and should be in the public  domain then what have they got to hide  Sky News understands an mi6 agent from  the Russia desk gave evidence as part of  the inquiry these sensitivities mean the  intelligence agencies and the Cabinet  Office are required to clear the report  ahead of publication that has already  happened which is why the committee says  the Prime Minister's sign-off should be  a formality one non-party political  source with a knowledge of the process  said the deadlines and timetables were a  gray area but added they couldn't see  any reason why number 10 shouldn't  publish the West is increasingly aware  of the threat posed by Russia and  arguments over the extent of its  interference in democracies like the UK  will continue for now though it appears  this latest contribution to the debate  will stay under wraps  brob Powell Sky News in Westminster
 

